        "original_id": "b194d399-a1ce-5703-99ea-8fdfede8bc80",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Yangzhou, Jiangsu Province, China, Yangtze River, Nanjing, Huai'an, Yancheng, Taizhou, Zhenjiang, Jiangyan District, Hanjiang District\n- Organizations: Gaomin Temple\n- Concepts: prefecture-level city, urban district, county-level city, romanization, Buddhist temple\n\nFacts:\n- Yangzhou was formerly romanized as Yangchow.\n- Yangzhou is a prefecture-level city in central Jiangsu Province, China.\n- Yangzhou sits on the north bank of the Yangtze River.\n- Yangzhou borders Nanjing to the southwest, Huai'an to the north, Yancheng to the northeast, Taizhou to the east, and Zhenjiang across the river to the south.\n- Until December 2012, Jiangyan District was a county-level city.\n- Jiangyan District is one of three urban districts of Taizhou in Jiangsu Province, China.\n- Gaomin Temple is a Buddhist temple in Hanjiang District of Yangzhou, Jiangsu Province, China.",
